Modifications (Dockerfile):
  /usr/share/doc/aptamer-raptgen/patches/ contains two audited patch files
  with these three changes:
  - raptgen/data.py: np.int -> int (NumPy >= 1.24 removed the alias).
  - raptgen/data.py: pHMM sampling weights normalize in float64 and correct
    the final value to an exact unit sum for NumPy 2.5.
  - raptgen/data.py: Result.get_bo_result raises; GPyOpt/GPy are not
    installed and scripts/bo.py is not shipped (Bayesian optimization excluded).
  Only scripts/encode.py, scripts/decode.py and scripts/real.py are shipped.

Bundled upstream example files (from the same commit, MIT):
  /opt/raptgen/data/sample/sample.fasta      (100 synthetic reads, AAAAA-20N-GGGGG)
  /opt/raptgen/data/sample/cnn_phmm_vae.mdl  (upstream sample model, ~0.9 MB)
  /opt/raptgen/data/sample/cnn_phmm_vae.csv  (its training-loss log)
No other model weights and no user data are included.

Bundled upstream data (same commit): data/real/A_4R.fastq, RaptGen paper dataset A.

Third-party Python packages:
  torch (2.14.1+cu126 and its NVIDIA CUDA runtime wheels, which are under the NVIDIA CUDA EULA),
  plus the hash-locked sets in /usr/share/doc/aptamer-raptgen/requirements.lock
  and requirements-s3.lock (boto3); each keeps its own license.
